# TESTING-HARNESS.md §2 `daemon …` · §3 the `daemon` snapshot field — the fault path with no
# pixels, so a machine with no compositor still proves that Fleet notices its daemon dying and
# reattaches to the replacement.
#
# `daemon-down.scenario` photographs the banner; this one is the structured half of the same
# behaviour and is part of the slice that rides `make test` (§7). Both exist because the
# reconnect is the one behaviour where a screenshot and a snapshot disagree about what "the
# banner is up" means: `daemon.link` moves the instant the link is lost, and the banner is
# painted a frame later.
fixture: one-repo
await idle 30000
assert screen == Hub && daemon.link == connected && daemon.attempt == 0
assert daemon.dismissed == false && daemon.restarted == false

# SIGKILL the run's own private fleetd. Nothing on the developer's machine is signalled.
daemon kill
await daemon.link == lost 30000
assert screen == Hub
dump lost

# The app reattaches on its own once the daemon is back, and says that it restarted.
daemon restart
await daemon.link == reconnected 60000
assert daemon.restarted == true && screen == Hub
await idle 30000
assert idle.idle == true
dump recovered
quit
